{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34675912",
      "title": "Fetching Expenses (via loader())",
      "lectureOrder": 68,
      "videoOrder": 62,
      "sourceHash": "499985f9f39dc4b6913ebbcdf4a56d3fdc99f4fa4a8a38c07b89043b2d1329f2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.08,
          "en": "So now that we're successfully storing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.08,
          "end": 5.67,
          "en": "our expenses in a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.67,
          "end": 9.57,
          "en": "let's also add some logic to fetch expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.57,
          "end": 12.81,
          "en": "because at the moment in my expenses list component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.81,
          "end": 16.17,
          "en": "I am outputting expenses which are hard coded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.17,
          "end": 18.72,
          "en": "into the expenses.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.72,
          "end": 21.42,
          "en": "There I got these dummy expenses which are being output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.42,
          "end": 23.73,
          "en": "and I wanna move away from those,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.73,
          "end": 27.07,
          "en": "and use the expenses from my database instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.07,
          "end": 30.75,
          "en": "Now for that, I'll remove these dummy expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.75,
          "end": 34.5,
          "en": "and no longer pass those to expenses list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.5,
          "end": 38.19,
          "en": "Instead here, we'll soon use data provided by our loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.19,
          "end": 41.58,
          "en": "and that's therefore what we add as the next step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.58,
          "end": 44.37,
          "en": "Here in expenses.jsx, we export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.37,
          "end": 48.42,
          "en": "an async function called loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.42,
          "end": 51.36,
          "en": "And of course I did introduce you to loaders already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.36,
          "end": 54.36,
          "en": "in the Remix Essentials course section as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.36,
          "end": 56.16,
          "en": "A loader is a special function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.16,
          "end": 59.28,
          "en": "which must be named loader because Remix will look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.28,
          "end": 62.88,
          "en": "for this name, and Remix will call this function for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.88,
          "end": 67.2,
          "en": "if it encounters a get request that reaches this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.2,
          "end": 70.11,
          "en": "so slash expenses in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.11,
          "end": 73.14,
          "en": "Then Remix will call this loader function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.14,
          "end": 75.96000000000001,
          "en": "Remix will also pass some data to the loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 78.18,
          "en": "an object where you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.18,
          "end": 82.346,
          "en": "can get hold of the params that might be encoded in the URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.346,
          "end": 85.44,
          "en": "though that's not relevant for this route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.44,
          "end": 88.2,
          "en": "since it has no dynamic params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.2,
          "end": 91.89,
          "en": "And this object, which you get passed to the loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.89,
          "end": 95.67,
          "en": "also has a request property which contains a request object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.67,
          "end": 98.00999999999999,
          "en": "with more details about the request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.00999999999999,
          "end": 101.34,
          "en": "but here we also don't need this at the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.34,
          "end": 103.32,
          "en": "Instead here in this loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.32,
          "end": 106.41,
          "en": "I simply want to get my expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.41,
          "end": 110.22,
          "en": "And for that I'll go back to expenses.server.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.22,
          "end": 113.91,
          "en": "And there I'll export a new async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 117.24000000000001,
          "en": "called getExpenses, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.24000000000001,
          "end": 119.25,
          "en": "And this function should simply, well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.25,
          "end": 122.643,
          "en": "retrieve all expenses that are stored in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.48,
          "end": 125.34,
          "en": "By the way, at the moment, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.34,
          "end": 128.52,
          "en": "we don't have any users in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.52,
          "end": 130.71,
          "en": "so all expenses are visible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.71,
          "end": 133.71,
          "en": "and editable for and by everyone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.71,
          "end": 136.02,
          "en": "This will change in the next course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.02,
          "end": 137.82,
          "en": "once we add authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.82,
          "end": 141.06,
          "en": "But for the moment, this is the behavior we have and want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.06,
          "end": 143.76,
          "en": "So we have global expenses, and here we simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.76,
          "end": 147.333,
          "en": "wanna fetch all expenses that are stored in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.35,
          "end": 150.63,
          "en": "To do that, we'll again, use Prisma,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 152.61,
          "en": "which we are already importing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.61,
          "end": 155.541,
          "en": "because we already used it for adding expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.541,
          "end": 159.45,
          "en": "And here we again access the expense property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.45,
          "end": 162,
          "en": "And now instead of creating a new expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162,
          "end": 165.63,
          "en": "as we did it before, we simply call find many,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.63,
          "end": 169.89,
          "en": "a built in method that finds many expense entries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.89,
          "end": 173.37,
          "en": "And by default if you don't pass any extra configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.37,
          "end": 177.84,
          "en": "to find many, it will simply return all expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.84,
          "end": 181.71,
          "en": "You could pass an object to find many where you, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.71,
          "end": 183.45,
          "en": "can set up a where condition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.45,
          "end": 187.47,
          "en": "and filter by amount, or date, or anything else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.47,
          "end": 191.013,
          "en": "But here I won't set anywhere condition to get all expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.88,
          "end": 194.91,
          "en": "I will however, pass this object to find many",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.91,
          "end": 198.45,
          "en": "but not to set this wear key as I just explained",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.45,
          "end": 201.72,
          "en": "but to set the order by key, because Prisma also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.72,
          "end": 205.02,
          "en": "helps us order the results that are retrieved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.02,
          "end": 206.67000000000002,
          "en": "And here I'll set order by",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 206.67000000000002,
          "end": 210.27,
          "en": "to an object where you can then refer to any",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.27,
          "end": 215.07,
          "en": "of these model properties that you define in your schema to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.07,
          "end": 219.03,
          "en": "for example, order by the date, not date added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.03,
          "end": 222.69,
          "en": "but the date of the expense, which was entered by the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 222.69,
          "end": 227.1,
          "en": "and order by that date in descending order, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.1,
          "end": 230.97,
          "en": "so that the list of expenses you get back is already ordered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.97,
          "end": 233.49,
          "en": "such that the latest expense is at the top,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.49,
          "end": 235.323,
          "en": "is the first expense in the list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.292,
          "end": 239.79,
          "en": "So with that, I now wanna await this because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.79,
          "end": 242.19,
          "en": "find many also returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 242.19,
          "end": 247.19,
          "en": "which will eventually resolve to an array of expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.44,
          "end": 250.44,
          "en": "So therefore, here I get these expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 250.44,
          "end": 253.86,
          "en": "and I can then return these expenses here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 253.86,
          "end": 256.183,
          "en": "That's what I wanna do in getExpenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.97,
          "end": 262.17,
          "en": "I also wanna wrap this into a try catch block though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.17,
          "end": 266.16,
          "en": "because getting my expenses could fail, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.16,
          "end": 269.28,
          "en": "because the database is temporarily unavailable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 269.28,
          "end": 271.23,
          "en": "or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.23,
          "end": 273.93,
          "en": "And in that case, I wanna handle the error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 273.93,
          "end": 277.38,
          "en": "and for the moment I'll again just log it and throw it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.38,
          "end": 281.223,
          "en": "but we can change this error handling logic later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 282.42,
          "end": 287.137,
          "en": "So here I get my expenses and with that function to find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 287.137,
          "end": 291.27,
          "en": "back in expenses.jsx in this loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 291.27,
          "end": 294.93,
          "en": "I wanna call this getExpenses function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 294.93,
          "end": 298.743,
          "en": "So here I call getExpenses, this function we just defined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 299.64,
          "end": 302.22,
          "en": "And for that of course we also add an import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 302.22,
          "end": 304.59,
          "en": "where we import getExpenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 304.59,
          "end": 308.7,
          "en": "from this expenses.server file in the data folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 308.7,
          "end": 311.07,
          "en": "And then of course this returns a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 311.07,
          "end": 314.7,
          "en": "which we can await, so that we get these expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 314.7,
          "end": 317.253,
          "en": "and then ultimately we can return them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 318.18,
          "end": 319.56,
          "en": "And since this is all we're doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 319.56,
          "end": 321.63,
          "en": "we could also simplify this of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 321.63,
          "end": 325.56,
          "en": "and just return getExpenses and remove async here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.56,
          "end": 328.11,
          "en": "so that we simply return the promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 328.11,
          "end": 331.65,
          "en": "that is yielded by this getExpenses function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 331.65,
          "end": 333.72,
          "en": "GetExpenses will yield a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 333.72,
          "end": 335.157,
          "en": "because it's an async function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 335.157,
          "end": 337.98,
          "en": "and async functions always return promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 337.98,
          "end": 342.03,
          "en": "which then resolve to the data you return in that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 342.03,
          "end": 344.58,
          "en": "So here getExpenses will return a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 344.58,
          "end": 347.31,
          "en": "that resolves to this list of expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.31,
          "end": 350.13,
          "en": "And in expenses.js and in this loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 350.13,
          "end": 352.29,
          "en": "I therefore simply return that promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 352.29,
          "end": 355.32,
          "en": "which eventually yields the expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 355.32,
          "end": 357.42,
          "en": "And Remix will automatically wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 357.42,
          "end": 359.31,
          "en": "for that promise to resolve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 359.31,
          "end": 361.89,
          "en": "before it then renders this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 361.89,
          "end": 364.65,
          "en": "And in this component, in this route component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 364.65,
          "end": 367.95,
          "en": "or any component used by that component, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 367.95,
          "end": 372.27,
          "en": "you can use useLoaderData to access that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 372.27,
          "end": 375.008,
          "en": "Again, I mentioned it before, but it is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 375.008,
          "end": 378.78,
          "en": "UseLoaderData, like useActionData, can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 378.78,
          "end": 382.11,
          "en": "in any component, not just in the route component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 382.11,
          "end": 383.64,
          "en": "And it will then give you access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 383.64,
          "end": 386.13,
          "en": "to the closest loader that was called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 386.13,
          "end": 388.89,
          "en": "so to the data of that closest loader, which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 388.89,
          "end": 391.59,
          "en": "in this case of course is the loader in the same file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 392.94,
          "end": 396.57,
          "en": "So that will give us access to this data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 396.57,
          "end": 399.96,
          "en": "and therefore here, ultimately, we get our expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 399.96,
          "end": 402.69,
          "en": "because the data returned by our loader here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 402.69,
          "end": 405,
          "en": "is that list of expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 405,
          "end": 406.8,
          "en": "It is a promise that resolves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 406.8,
          "end": 409.26,
          "en": "to that array of expenses as I mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 409.26,
          "end": 411.78,
          "en": "And I also mentioned that Remix would",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 411.78,
          "end": 414.57,
          "en": "wait for that promise to resolve and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 414.57,
          "end": 418.14300000000003,
